action.instruction:
Revert the two unspecced socket changes; do not touch cred-server.spec.ts.

1) apps/runner/src/credentials/socket-dir.ts: restore socketPathFor to the D78 form:

    const key = createHash('sha256').update(`${runnerId}:${jobId}:${leaseEpoch}`).digest('hex').slice(0, 16);
    return join(dir, `${key}.sock`);

(16 hex + '.sock'; keep the rest of the file unchanged.)

2) apps/runner/src/daemon/daemon.ts: delete the silent relocation block (lines ~109-115):

    let socketDir = config.socketDir ?? defaultSocketDir(uid);
    if (Buffer.byteLength(socketPathFor(socketDir, identity.runnerId, 'j', 1)) > MAX_SOCKET_PATH_BYTES) {
      socketDir = join(process.cwd(), `.rs-${uid}`);
    }

replace it with

    const socketDir = config.socketDir ?? defaultSocketDir(uid);
    await ensureSocketDir(socketDir, uid);

so an over-long socketDir refuses the start with SocketDirError (the check inside ensureSocketDir already refuses paths over 100 bytes, and it uses the same fixed-width hash, so it is exact for any jobId). Drop the now-unused MAX_SOCKET_PATH_BYTES and socketPathFor from the '../credentials/socket-dir' import (keep defaultSocketDir, ensureSocketDir). No fallback to process.cwd(), os.tmpdir() or any other directory: the socket dir is config.socketDir or /tmp/koda-runner-<uid>, or the daemon does not start.

3) Verify: cd apps/runner && bun run test && bun run type-check && bun run lint. The unmodified cred-server.spec.ts test 'socket paths are 16 hex characters per (runner, job, epoch)' and test/unit/daemon-socket-dir.spec.ts must pass. Do not 'fix' the failure by updating cred-server.spec.ts to the 12-hex format. If a test machine's TMPDIR genuinely makes a socket path exceed 100 bytes, the remedy is a shorter socketDir (runner.json socketDir or a short TMPDIR), never a silent relocation.
